{
 "about": "Medallion at the centre of the left door leaf of the Garden Gate (plate 4, 'North Side of Garden Gate'), left half, drawn by hand as band centre lines while viewing the University of Manchester copy of the 1786 engravings online (PR-CHCR-00457, image 26). Only these hand-drawn control points are used; no pixels of that scan. Coordinates are that scan's pixels. Four strap arms on a hatched ground: tulip U-straps above and below whose tips curl out into horns, horizontal tulips left and right, C-scrolls with curls in the corners, a teardrop bead, and a raised ring with a central boss. The right half is the mirror image. The straps stand on the plain door face; the hatched ground between them is left at the face. Positions are registered to the Palace Museum album with the axis at its measured centre (album x 2384); each band is then moved as a whole (shape unchanged, at most 3.5 scan px) onto the album's strap, since the two printings differ by a pixel or two.",
